    "items": [
      {
        "text": "Marissa Roy is a deputy attorney general in the California Attorney General's office. She says she previously worked in the LA City Attorney’s Office on wage theft cases and represented LA County in litigation against the Trump administration. She helped build the state's case against Meta that ended in a $17-billion settlement. She also says she obtained a half-million-dollar judgment against a landlord.",
        "cites": [1, 2, 3],
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "Marissa Roy is a deputy attorney general in the California Attorney General's office.",
            "cites": [1]
          },
          {
            "text": "She says she previously worked in the LA City Attorney’s Office on wage theft cases and represented LA County in litigation against the Trump administration.",
            "cites": [2]
          },
          {
            "text": "She helped build the state's case against Meta that ended in a $17-billion settlement.",
            "cites": [3]
          },
          {
            "text": "She also says she obtained a half-million-dollar judgment against a landlord.",
            "cites": [2]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Her campaign says she would expand the office’s enforcement of workers’ and renters’ rights, sue corporate polluters, and challenge the Trump administration. She supports diversion programs over incarceration and a liability audit by the City Controller.",
